[[File:Operation_Castle_-_Romeo_001.jpg|thumb|125px|A [[w:nuclear holocaust|nuclear holocaust]] is often associated with [[w:Armageddon|Armageddon]]]].
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|he|en}} {{term|הר מגידו|lang=he||tr=har megiddo}}, used in [http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Bible_%28World_English%29/Revelation#Chapter_16 Revelation 16:16], referring to [[w:Tel Megiddo|Mount Megiddo]], the place of the last battle at the [[w:Last Judgment|Last Judgment]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɛdən}}
* {{hyphenation|Ar|ma|ged|don}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The place where the final battle will be fought between the forces of [[good]] and [[evil]].
# The scene of a decisive conflict on a great scale.
# Any great and crucial conflict.

